WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.568
And as the war in Ukraine drags

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.269
on, opponents of President

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:05.672
Vladimir Putin face a risky decision.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.273
Do they challenge the Kremlin

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.275
and speak out against the war?

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:09.809
Well, Putin's

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.244
critics face danger,

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.279
even death, for speaking out.

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.181
Details from CNN's senior

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.549
international correspondent

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.451
Matthew Chance.

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:22.222
Yeah, yeah,

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.125
I guess I

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:30.630
It takes a certain type of bravery

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.800
to stand up to the Kremlin

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.768
across the country.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.270
This using arrests and beatings

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.339
to crush dissent

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.441
against the Ukrainian forces and

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:44.778
some anti-war

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:47.614
protesters even drafted into the army

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.617
in a cruel punishment for pacifism.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.921
So it now 60 P of any

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.289
political opposition.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.657
Always a risky business

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.025
in Putin's Russia.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.594
He's now essentially outlaws who

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.797
with prominent opposition leaders

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.099
like Ilya Yashin,

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.767
recently sentenced to eight

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.004
and a half years in jail for criticizing

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:11.738
the conflict

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.408
This will

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.677
all end soon, he shouts in defiance.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:18.812
But there's

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.181
little real reason for optimism.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.751
This was Vladimir Kara-Murza,

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.453
another leading Russian opposition

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:29.222
figure in Moscow, back in 2015

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.991
after surviving a suspected poisoning

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.961
at the hands of Kremlin agents.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.663
He was allegedly poisoned again

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:39.199
in 2017 and survived that too

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.702
only to be imprisoned last April

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.304
on charges

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.573
ranging from disobeying the police

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.174
to treason.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.676
The price of silence

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.411
Kara-Murza wrote from jail

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:54.714
was simply unacceptable.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.851
That the price

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.752
of speaking out against Putin's

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:03.056
Russia is extraordinarily high too.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.791
Case in point

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:07.560
the former president of Georgia country

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.930
lost a brief war with Russia in 2008.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.633
My small nation will never give up

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.802
freedom will never give a square mile.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.836
Two years ago,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.271
Mikhail Saakashvili

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.039
was imprisoned in Georgia

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.407
and what his supporters say

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.276
were trumped up charges.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.312
Now this one time Putin foe is at

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.015
death's door, allegedly poisoned too,

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:31.050
and accusing Moscow

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.553
of orchestrating his plight.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.955
The Kremlin rejects the allegation,

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.690
but his family are adamant

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.559
to put somebody in this state

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.194
after just a year of imprisonment.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.129
That's that was unexpected.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:44.864
But for

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.799
years, Kremlin critics

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.868
have been ruthlessly silenced.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.670
Like Anna Politkovskaya,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.938
Russia's most prominent

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.973
investigative journalist,

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.508
until she was gunned down

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.778
in her Moscow apartment building in 2006

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.916
Or Alexander Litvinenko,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.750
a former Russian

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.218
FSB agent,

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.520
poisoned in London in the same year

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.324
with a radioactive isotope in 2018.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:14.060
A former Russian spy, Sergei Skripal,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.395
and his daughter

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.130
were poisoned in Britain

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.232
using a potent nerve agent.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.567
They survived

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.503
propaganda

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.338
for years before.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.440
Russia's leading opposition figure,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.808
Boris Nemtsov,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.176
was shot dead

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.412
within sight of the Kremlin.

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:32.879
Of course,

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.214
the Kremlin denies

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.449
any connection to any crime,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.687
but exiled, jailed, poisoned or killed.

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:43.990
Is how so many of Putin's critics

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.925
seem to act.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:48.628
Matthew Chance, CNN, London.

